rding). Branch B touches no\n  Platform Operator code and therefore needs no onboarding.\n- Llama Stack and Dashboard both have architecture-context files (in platform,\n  Konflux-onboarded) — no onboarding epics generated for them.\n- Milvus itself is not a RHAI Jira component; work to deploy and productize it\n  is assigned to the Platform Operator canonical component as the most-relevant\n  name.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n   Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria,\n   and no Non-Functional Requirements. Epic acceptance criteria were derived\n   from the HLRs and problem statement; team assignments were taken from\n   architecture context where available.\n2. **Assumed team assignments**: no owner is stated for Platform Operator\n   (assigned \"RHOAI Platform\") or Documentation (assigned \"RHOI Documentation\"\n   work assigned to \"RHOAI Documentation\") — verify with the strategy owner\n   before execution.\n3. **Platform Operator in-platform status**: the onboarding chain in Branch A\n   rests on Platform Operator lacking an architecture-context file. If the\n   operator already ships in the platform (context file simply missing), the\n   onboarding chain collapses into the general implementation epic.\n4. **Scope trap — \"productized images\"**: HLR-2's productized-images clause\n   implies image build/release infrastructure for Milvus. This is folded into\n   BRANCH-A-E005's scope; if a separate midstream image repository turns out to\n   be required, split it out at implementation planning time.\n5. **Docs priority exception applied**: the docs epics are P1 (strategy\n   frontmatter priority Major → P1) even though HLR-5 is labeled P2. This is\n   the rule-mandated docs-authoring priority exception, not an inconsistency —\n   flagged for human verification.\n6. **No priority inversions detected**: the onboarding chain is P0 because it\n   exists