{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-88a0cf8a-edb8-42c4-a8d2-da0ef18cbcd5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b5cf650ed7de0bd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9007-7ohyjd6a/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9007-E001.md","content":"# Decide first supported vector store posture (managed vs external)\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's gating open question: which vector\nstore posture the platform productizes first — a platform-managed vector\ndatabase (operator-deployed Milvus with productized images) or an\nexternal-connection-only posture (customers connect their own managed vector\nservice). It produces a documented evaluation and a single recorded decision\nthat determines the existence and shape of all downstream implementation work\nfor RAG workloads on Llama Stack.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Evaluate the platform-managed posture (operator-deployed Milvus,\n  productized/supported images, platform-owned lifecycle) against the\n  external-connection-only posture (sanctioned registration of\n  customer-managed vector stores per project).\n- Weigh the evaluation criteria named in the strategy: supportability cost,\n  disconnected-environment viability, and time-to-market.\n- Ground the evaluation in readable evidence: Milvus operational\n  characteristics and dependency footprint, the Llama Stack vector/RAG\n  provider surface, and the platform's existing operator and Dashboard\n  integration patterns.\n- Record the decision with rationale, including which downstream conditional\n  branch (managed path or external path) the outcome selects.\n- Obtain stakeholder acceptance of the decision (this is a product posture\n  call, not a purely technical one).\n\nOut of scope: implementing either posture; deciding embedding model selection\nand lifecycle (separate strategy); shipping both postures in the same release.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written evaluation exists that compares the platform-managed posture and\n  the external-connection-only posture against explicitly stated criteria:\n  supportability cost, disconnected-environment viability, and\n  time-to-market.\n- The evaluation is grounded in citable evidence (Milvus project\n  characteristics, Llama Stack provider capabilities, platform integration\n  patterns) rather than assertion alone.\n- A single posture decision is recorded with rationale traceable to the\n  evaluation.\n- The recorded decision identifies which conditional downstream branch of\n  work proceeds.\n- Stakeholder sign-off on the decision is recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A decision is reached, with a documented evaluation, on the\n  first supported vector store posture. This epic is the sole coverage for\n  HLR-1.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49150,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b05929c334cc90fa","agent_id":"af8f777e8b5c59276","session_id":"124e4662-1fae-4b45-93d6-fde3aa562cb7","uuid":"6ce4dfea-ceee-4de6-9b16-e5622565a5f5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:47:22.481Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9007 strategy"}
