{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ffbb6979-d703-4def-97d8-475af7b0251d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-934b14bf0da8f3de","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9007-7ohyjd6a/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002.md","content":"# Per-project external vector store connection registration and management UI\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the external-connection-only posture's core capability: data\nscientists can register an external vector store connection per project with\nvalidated connectivity, and manage those connections through the Dashboard.\nThis epic covers both the registration capability and its connection\nmanagement UI — they are the same Dashboard surface for the same team, so\nthey are one capability at the higher of the two HLR priorities.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add external vector store connections as a registerable, project-scoped\n  connection type in the Dashboard's connection management surface\n  (create, edit, delete, list).\n- Implement connectivity validation on registration: the Dashboard verifies\n  the connection parameters reach the external vector store and reports a\n  pass/fail result with an actionable message on failure.\n- Store connections per project, consistent with the Dashboard's\n  project-scoped resource model (the Dashboard reads and writes Kubernetes\n  resources and owns no data plane).\n- Keep validation generic across external vector store providers (endpoint\n  and credential connectivity checking), with the sanctioned-provider list\n  and store-specific parameter handling resolved at implementation time.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A data scientist can register an external vector store connection scoped\n  to a project, and can list, edit, and delete it from the Dashboard.\n- Registration runs a connectivity validation whose pass/fail outcome is\n  surfaced to the user.\n- An invalid or incomplete connection produces an actionable error message\n  identifying the problem.\n- Connections are isolated per project (a connection registered in one\n  project is not visible or usable in another).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — external-path clause: \"data scientists can register an\n  external vector store connection per project with validated connectivity.\"\n- **HLR-4 (P1)** — external-path clause: \"connection management UI for the\n  external path.\" Consolidated with HLR-2 into this single epic because both\n  describe the same Dashboard connection-management surface for the same\n  component and team; the epic takes the higher priority (P0).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":60778,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b05929c334cc90fa","agent_id":"af8f777e8b5c59276","session_id":"124e4662-1fae-4b45-93d6-fde3aa562cb7","uuid":"069f5ff3-063a-4ab7-9d61-2a338cc50c36","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:50:28.860Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9007 strategy"}
