{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9885d43c38048477","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-B-E002\n3\ttitle: Per-project external vector store connection registration and management UI\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the external-connection-only posture is not selected, per-project\n16\t    external connection registration is not delivered; the managed branch delivers\n17\t    HLR-2 and HLR-4 through the Platform Operator and Dashboard deploy-and-manage\n18\t    UI instead.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 7\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Per-project external vector store connection registration and management UI\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tDelivers the external-connection-only posture's core capability: data\n40\tscientists can register an external vector store connection per project with\n41\tvalidated connectivity, and manage those connections through the Dashboard.\n42\tThis epic covers both the registration capability and its connection\n43\tmanagement UI — they are the same Dashboard surface for the same team, so\n44\tthey are one capability at the higher of the two HLR priorities.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Add external vector store connections as a registerable, project-scoped\n49\t  connection type in the Dashboard's connection management surface\n50\t  (create, edit, delete, list).\n51\t- Implement connectivity validation on registration: the Dashboard verifies\n52\t  the connection parameters reach the external vector store and reports a\n53\t  pass/fail result with an actionable message on failure.\n54\t- Store connections per project, consistent with the Dashboard's\n55\t  project-scoped resource model (the Dashboard reads and writes Kubernetes\n56\t  resources and owns no data plane).\n57\t- Keep validation generic across external vector store providers (endpoint\n58\t  and credential connectivity checking), with the sanctioned-provider list\n59\t  and store-specific parameter handling resolved at implementation time.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- A data scientist can register an external vector store connection scoped\n64\t  to a project, and can list, edit, and delete it from the Dashboard.\n65\t- Registration runs a connectivity validation whose pass/fail outcome is\n66\t  surfaced to the user.\n67\t- An invalid or incomplete connection produces an actionable error message\n68\t  identifying the problem.\n69\t- Connections are isolated per project (a connection registered in one\n70\t  project is not visible or usable in another).\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — external-path clause: \"data scientists can register an\n75\t  external vector store connection per project with validated connectivity.\"\n76\t- **HLR-4 (P1)** — external-path clause: \"connection management UI for the\n77\t  external path.\" Consolidated with HLR-2 into this single epic because both\n78\t  describe the same Dashboard connection-management surface for the same\n79\t  component and team; the epic takes the higher priority (P0).\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9675dbf1e0526aff","agent_id":"aa6cd019c2423aa9a","session_id":"124e4662-1fae-4b45-93d6-fde3aa562cb7","uuid":"d626b78c-832e-44b8-bf50-008eebc3b165","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:55:20.386Z","tool_result_meta":[