9\trepo-onboarding and konflux-onboarding). Critical path 5 fits the\n70\t\"medium with new component\" heuristic (4-5).\n71\t\n72\tHowever, **the DAG is missing the Rule 6 edge `BRANCH-A-E002 → BRANCH-A-E005`**.\n73\tRule 6: \"repo-onboarding → general implementation of onboarded component\n74\talways serial (code needs repo).\" BRANCH-A-E005 is the Platform Operator\n75\tgeneral implementation; its operator code lands in the midstream repository\n76\tthat BRANCH-A-E002 creates — its own ai-signals rationale presupposes it\n77\t(\"Midstream repository is platform-owned and clonable\"). A-E005's\n78\t`dependencies` list only E001 and A-E003, and the summary DAG justification\n79\ttable conspicuously omits any A-E002 → A-E005 row (it addresses A-E002 ∥\n80\tA-E003 and the absent A-E004 → A-E005 edge, but never A-E002 → A-E005). As\n81\tdrawn, A-E005 can be scheduled before the repository it must commit to exists.\n82\tThis is a missing edge where a hard artifact dependency exists — a critical\n83\tissue. Note Rule 10's parallel mandate covers only the konflux-onboarding ↔\n84\tgeneral pairing; it does not exempt the repo-onboarding → general edge. Fix:\n85\tadd `RHAISTRAT-9007-BRANCH-A-E002` to A-E005's `dependencies` and the\n86\tcorresponding edge to the summary DAG.\n87\t\n88\tOther edges verified as justified: A-E002 → A-E004 (Rule 5), A-E003 → A-E005\n89\t(Rule 9), A-E005 → A-E006/A-E007 (Rules 12/13 — the Llama Stack and Dashboard\n90\twork builds against the managed-store CR/interface A-E005 produces, a\n91\tbuild-against artifact, not a digest/URL configuration reference), all Branch A\n92\timplementations → A-E008 and Branch B implementations → B-E004 (Rule 11),\n93\tB-E002 → B-E003 (Rule 13 — the wiring builds against the registered-connection\n94\tresource format). No circular dependencies; no cross-branch edges (correct —\n95\tbranches are mutually exclusive).\n96\t\n97\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n98\tEvery epic is a single component/team tuple (verifi