rding chain collapses into the general implementation epic.\n195\t4. **Scope trap — \"productized images\"**: HLR-2's productized-images clause\n196\t   implies image build/release infrastructure for Milvus. This is folded into\n197\t   BRANCH-A-E005's scope; if a separate midstream image repository turns out to\n198\t   be required, split it out at implementation planning time.\n199\t5. **Docs priority exception applied**: the docs epics are P1 (strategy\n200\t   frontmatter priority Major → P1) even though HLR-5 is labeled P2. This is\n201\t   the rule-mandated docs-authoring priority exception, not an inconsistency —\n202\t   flagged for human verification.\n203\t6. **No priority inversions detected**: the onboarding chain is P0 because it\n204\t   exists solely to enable the P0 HLR-2 operator implementation.\n205\t\n206\t## Tiered Delivery\n207\t\n208\tNot applicable. The fork here is an internal product decision with bounded\n209\toutcomes (modeled as conditional branches), not an external dependency with\n210\tuncertain timing. Shipping both postures in the same release is explicitly out\n211\tof scope, so no partial-value tiering across postures is offered; within each\n212\tbranch, P1 epics (Llama Stack wiring, Dashboard UI) are independently\n213\tdeferrable features behind the P0 core.\n214\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-981a0a441a33b118","agent_id":"a6e60a1d191b3c305","session_id":"124e4662-1fae-4b45-93d6-fde3aa562cb7","uuid":"ae546707-2f27-4332-af22-729d7e743b01","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:02:18.862Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b86fe190d95afd37","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
