{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a779d5caf0b9ea2a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9007-E001\n3\ttitle: Decide first supported vector store posture (managed vs external)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Decide first supported vector store posture (managed vs external)\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's gating open question: which vector\n30\tstore posture the platform productizes first — a platform-managed vector\n31\tdatabase (operator-deployed Milvus with productized images) or an\n32\texternal-connection-only posture (customers connect their own managed vector\n33\tservice). It produces a documented evaluation and a single recorded decision\n34\tthat determines the existence and shape of all downstream implementation work\n35\tfor RAG workloads on Llama Stack.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Evaluate the platform-managed posture (operator-deployed Milvus,\n40\t  productized/supported images, platform-owned lifecycle) against the\n41\t  external-connection-only posture (sanctioned registration of\n42\t  customer-managed vector stores per project).\n43\t- Weigh the evaluation criteria named in the strategy: supportability cost,\n44\t  disconnected-environment viability, and time-to-market.\n45\t- Ground the evaluation in readable evidence: Milvus operational\n46\t  characteristics and dependency footprint, the Llama Stack vector/RAG\n47\t  provider surface, and the platform's existing operator and Dashboard\n48\t  integration patterns.\n49\t- Record the decision with rationale, including which downstream conditional\n50\t  branch (managed path or external path) the outcome selects.\n51\t- Obtain stakeholder acceptance of the decision (this is a product posture\n52\t  call, not a purely technical one).\n53\t\n54\tOut of scope: implementing either posture; deciding embedding model selection\n55\tand lifecycle (separate strategy); shipping both postures in the same release.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A written evaluation exists that compares the platform-managed posture and\n60\t  the external-connection-only posture against explicitly stated criteria:\n61\t  supportability cost, disconnected-environment viability, and\n62\t  time-to-market.\n63\t- The evaluation is grounded in citable evidence (Milvus project\n64\t  characteristics, Llama Stack provider capabilities, platform integration\n65\t  patterns) rather than assertion alone.\n66\t- A single posture decision is recorded with rationale traceable to the\n67\t  evaluation.\n68\t- The recorded decision identifies which conditional downstream branch of\n69\t  work proceeds.\n70\t- Stakeholder sign-off on the decision is recorded.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A decision is reached, with a documented evaluation, on the\n75\t  first supported vector store posture. This epic is the sole coverage for\n76\t  HLR-1.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-981a0a441a33b118","agent_id":"a6e60a1d191b3c305","session_id":"124e4662-1fae-4b45-93d6-fde3aa562cb7","uuid":"2998ed4a-9a6a-4a9e-9196-3d4820f1ded7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:02:28.084Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a779d5caf0b9ea2a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
