{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9bd7d691fe252bc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n3\tepic_count: 11\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9007 (Bring-your-own vector database for RAG workloads)\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Outcome\n13\t\n14\tNot below-threshold: the strategy carries an explicit, strategy-author-classified\n15\topen question (managed Milvus vs external-connection-only posture) whose answer\n16\tchanges which epics exist for HLR-2 through HLR-5, and the scope spans three\n17\tcomponents (Llama Stack, Dashboard, Platform Operator) across multiple teams.\n18\tNot docs-only: code changes are required in at least two components under\n19\teither outcome. Full decomposition performed.\n20\t\n21\t## Decomposition Approach\n22\t\n23\tThe single qualifying unknown (Open Question 1 / HLR-1) is the posture\n24\tdecision: platform-managed vector store (operator-deployed Milvus) versus\n25\texternal-connection-only. It has exactly two bounded outcomes, so it is modeled\n26\tas one main-plan Investigation epic (E001) with two conditional branches:\n27\t\n28\t- **Branch A — platform-managed**: Platform Operator deploys Milvus with\n29\t  productized images; Llama Stack consumes the managed store; Dashboard gets a\n30\t  deploy-and-manage UI.\n31\t- **Branch B — external-connection-only**: Dashboard provides per-project\n32\t  external connection registration with validated connectivity; Llama Stack\n33\t  consumes a registered connection; Dashboard connection management UI.\n34\t\n35\tAll other unclear passages (CRD shapes, wiring mechanisms, image build\n36\tstrategy, sanctioned store list) are implementation details captured as\n37\tacceptance criteria on the relevant epics, not investigations — they do not\n38\tchange which epics exist. Milvus viability/supportability is folded into the\n39\tE001 evaluation itself (same evaluation, same deliverable — not split into a\n40\tseparate investigation).\n41\t\n42\t## Epic List\n43\t\n44\t### Main plan\n45\t\n46\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n47\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n48\t| E001 | Decide first supported vector store posture (managed vs external) | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | Llama Stack | P0 |\n49\t\n50\t### Branch A — platform-managed (operator-deployed Milvus)\n51\t\n52\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n53\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n54\t| BRANCH-A-E002 | Onboard Platform Operator midstream repository | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n55\t| BRANCH-A-E003 | License validation for operator and Milvus dependency trees | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n56\t| BRANCH-A-E004 | Konflux onboarding for Platform Operator repository | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n57\t| BRANCH-A-E005 | Managed vector store deployment via Platform Operator with productized images | Implementation | RHOAI Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n58\t| BRANCH-A-E006 | Llama Stack RAG provider wiring for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | Llama Stack | P1 |\n59\t| BRANCH-A-E007 | Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n60\t| BRANCH-A-E008 | Product documentation for the managed vector store posture | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | Documentation | P1 |\n61\t\n62\t### Branch B — external-connection-only\n63\t\n64\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n65\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n66\t| BRANCH-B-E002 | Per-project external vector store connection registration and management UI | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P0 |\n67\t| BRANCH-B-E003 | Llama Stack RAG provider wiring for registered external connections | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | Llama Stack | P1 |\n68\t| BRANCH-B-E004 | Product documentation for the external-connection posture | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | Documentation | P1 |\n69\t\n70\tMain-plan epic count: 1. Total including branch epics: 11. Main-plan critical\n71\tpath length: 1 (E001 alone). Longest path through a branch: 5\n72\t(E001 → BRANCH-A-E003 → BRANCH-A-E005 → BRANCH-A-E006 → BRANCH-A-E008).\n73\t\n74\t## Dependency DAG\n75\t\n76\t```mermaid\n77\tgraph TD\n78\t    E001[\"E001 Posture decision (Investigation)\"]\n79\t\n80\t    subgraph BranchA[\"Branch A — platform-managed\"]\n81\t        AE002[\"A-E002 repo-onboarding\"]\n82\t        AE003[\"A-E003 license-validation\"]\n83\t        AE004[\"A-E004 konflux-onboarding\"]\n84\t        AE005[\"A-E005 managed store via Platform Operator\"]\n85\t        AE006[\"A-E006 Llama Stack managed provider\"]\n86\t        AE007[\"A-E007 Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI\"]\n87\t        AE008[\"A-E008 managed-posture docs\"]\n88\t    end\n89\t\n90\t    subgraph BranchB[\"Branch B — external-connection-only\"]\n91\t        BE002[\"B-E002 Dashboard connection registration + UI\"]\n92\t        BE003[\"B-E003 Llama Stack external provider\"]\n93\t        BE004[\"B-E004 external-posture docs\"]\n94\t    end\n95\t\n96\t    E001 --> AE002\n97\t    E001 --> AE003\n98\t    E001 --> AE005\n99\t    E001 --> AE006\n100\t    E001 --> AE007\n101\t    E001 --> AE008\n102\t    AE002 --> AE004\n103\t    AE002 --> AE005\n104\t    AE003 --> AE005\n105\t    AE005 --> AE006\n106\t    AE005 --> AE007\n107\t    AE002 --> AE008\n108\t    AE003 --> AE008\n109\t    AE004 --> AE008\n110\t    AE005 --> AE008\n111\t    AE006 --> AE008\n112\t    AE007 --> AE008\n113\t\n114\t    E001 --> BE002\n115\t    E001 --> BE003\n116\t    E001 --> BE004\n117\t    BE002 --> BE003\n118\t    BE002 --> BE004\n119\t    BE003 --> BE004\n120\t```\n121\t\n122\tNote: BRANCH-A-E004 (konflux-onboarding) deliberately has **no** edge to\n123\tBRANCH-A-E005 — they run in parallel (Rule 10); the coupling is enforced by the\n124\t\"build pipeline green\" acceptance criterion on BRANCH-A-E005 (Rule 25).\n125\t\n126\t## DAG Justification\n127\t\n128\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n129\t|------|------|-----------|\n130\t| E001 → all branch epics | 3 | Posture decision determines existence and shape of all HLR-2..HLR-5 work; true gate with `remove` impact — the non-selected branch does not exist. Bounded (2 outcomes) → conditional branches. |\n131\t| BRANCH-A-E002 → BRANCH-A-E004 | 5 | repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding always serial; the pipeline needs the repo. |\n132\t| BRANCH-A-E002 → BRANCH-A-E005 | 6 | repo-onboarding → general implementation of the onboarded component always serial; the operator code for the managed vector store lands in the midstream repository A-E002 creates. (Rule 10 exempts only the konflux-onboarding ↔ general pairing, not this edge.) |\n133\t| BRANCH-A-E003 → BRANCH-A-E005 | 9 | license-validation → general implementation serial; license failures would change the dependency set and approach. |\n134\t| (none) BRANCH-A-E004 → BRANCH-A-E005 | 10 | konflux-onboarding ∥ general implementation parallel by rule; enforced via \"build pipeline green\" AC on A-E005 (Rule 25), never a DAG edge. |\n135\t| BRANCH-A-E005 → BRANCH-A-E006 | 12/13 | The Llama Stack provider wiring builds against the managed-store interface the Platform Operator work produces (framework → consumer serial). |\n136\t| BRANCH-A-E005 → BRANCH-A-E007 | 13 | The Dashboard integration builds against the managed vector store resource/interface produced by the operator work (Dashboard reads/writes CRs per architecture context). |\n137\t| BRANCH-A-E006 ∥ BRANCH-A-E007 | 14 | Different components/repos (Llama Stack vs Dashboard), no shared artifacts — parallel. |\n138\t| BRANCH-A-E002/E003/E004/E005/E006/E007 → BRANCH-A-E008 | 11 | docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. |\n139\t| BRANCH-B-E002 → BRANCH-B-E003 | 13 | The Llama Stack wiring consumes the connection registration format/artifact the Dashboard work produces (build-against artifact, not a mere config reference — \"without hand-editing distribution configs\" means the wiring integrates with the registration mechanism). |\n140\t| BRANCH-B-E002, BRANCH-B-E003 → BRANCH-B-E004 | 11 | docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation epics in the branch. |\n141\t| BRANCH-A-E002 ∥ BRANCH-A-E003 | 7 | repo-onboarding and license-validation have independent inputs — parallel. |\n142\t| BRANCH-A-E003 ∥ BRANCH-A-E004 | 8 | license-validation and konflux-onboarding parallel; config does not depend on specific deps. |\n143\t\n144\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n145\t\n146\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n147\t|-----|----------|---------|\n148\t| HLR-1 (posture decision with documented evaluation) | P0 | E001 |\n149\t| HLR-2 (managed deployment OR external connection registration) | P0 | Branch A: BRANCH-A-E005 · Branch B: BRANCH-B-E002 |\n150\t| HLR-3 (Llama Stack consumes chosen store as RAG provider) | P1 | Branch A: BRANCH-A-E006 · Branch B: BRANCH-B-E003 |\n151\t| HLR-4 (Dashboard exposes chosen integration) | P1 | Branch A: BRANCH-A-E007 · Branch B: BRANCH-B-E002 (consolidated, see below) |\n152\t| HLR-5 (documentation for shipped posture) | P2 | Branch A: BRANCH-A-E008 · Branch B: BRANCH-B-E004 |\n153\t\n154\tFull coverage: every HLR maps to at least one epic in **each** branch, so\n155\teither investigation outcome satisfies the strategy.\n156\t\n157\t**HLR consolidation note (Branch B):** HLR-2 (external path: \"data scientists\n158\tcan register an external vector store connection per project with validated\n159\tconnectivity\") and HLR-4 (external path: \"connection management UI\") describe\n160\tthe same Dashboard surface for the same component and team — HLR-4 is the\n161\tpre