uce a go/no-go recommendation for the managed posture's dependency set.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A license scan report exists covering both the operator and the Milvus\n57\t  dependency trees.\n58\t- Milvus (Apache-2.0) and its transitive dependencies are confirmed\n59\t  compatible with productization, or every incompatibility is documented with\n60\t  a remediation option.\n61\t- A recorded go/no-go recommendation exists for the managed posture's\n62\t  dependency set.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — enabling work: the managed-path clause requires\n67\t  \"productized images\"; license clearance is the prerequisite for productizing\n68\t  the Milvus-based dependency set.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a2ebb02c99ded2f","agent_id":"a32686bd1f194396e","session_id":"124e4662-1fae-4b45-93d6-fde3aa562cb7","uuid":"273c9501-c760-4afc-b381-8863d0fd0a67","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:06:18.079Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dc66639491cdb43","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9007 decomposition"}
