face\n50\t  (create, edit, delete, list).\n51\t- Implement connectivity validation on registration: the Dashboard verifies\n52\t  the connection parameters reach the external vector store and reports a\n53\t  pass/fail result with an actionable message on failure.\n54\t- Store connections per project, consistent with the Dashboard's\n55\t  project-scoped resource model (the Dashboard reads and writes Kubernetes\n56\t  resources and owns no data plane).\n57\t- Keep validation generic across external vector store providers (endpoint\n58\t  and credential connectivity checking), with the sanctioned-provider list\n59\t  and store-specific parameter handling resolved at implementation time.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- A data scientist can register an external vector store connection scoped\n64\t  to a project, and can list, edit, and delete it from the Dashboard.\n65\t- Registration runs a connectivity validation whose pass/fail outcome is\n66\t  surfaced to the user.\n67\t- An invalid or incomplete connection produces an actionable error message\n68\t  identifying the problem.\n69\t- Connections are isolated per project (a connection registered in one\n70\t  project is not visible or usable in another).\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — external-path clause: \"data scientists can register an\n75\t  external vector store connection per project with validated connectivity.\"\n76\t- **HLR-4 (P1)** — external-path clause: \"connection management UI for the\n77\t  external path.\" Consolidated with HLR-2 into this single epic because both\n78\t  describe the same Dashboard connection-management surface for the same\n79\t  component and team; the epic takes the higher priority (P0).\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a2ebb02c99ded2f","agent_id":"a32686bd1f194396e","session_id":"124e4662-1fae-4b45-93d6-fde3aa562cb7","uuid":"c1823889-45ba-4ec0-88a8-e2b6dcb19164","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:06:26.070Z","tool_result_meta":[