{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b893e9aba458e232","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9007\n3\tepic_count: 11\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9007 (Bring-your-own vector database for RAG workloads)\n10\t\n11\t## Triage Outcome\n12\t\n13\tNot below-threshold: the strategy carries an explicit, strategy-author-classified\n14\topen question (managed Milvus vs external-connection-only posture) whose answer\n15\tchanges which epics exist for HLR-2 through HLR-5, and the scope spans three\n16\tcomponents (Llama Stack, Dashboard, Platform Operator) across multiple teams.\n17\tNot docs-only: code changes are required in at least two components under\n18\teither outcome. Full decomposition performed.\n19\t\n20\t## Decomposition Approach\n21\t\n22\tThe single qualifying unknown (Open Question 1 / HLR-1) is the posture\n23\tdecision: platform-managed vector store (operator-deployed Milvus) versus\n24\texternal-connection-only. It has exactly two bounded outcomes, so it is modeled\n25\tas one main-plan Investigation epic (E001) with two conditional branches:\n26\t\n27\t- **Branch A — platform-managed**: Platform Operator deploys Milvus with\n28\t  productized images; Llama Stack consumes the managed store; Dashboard gets a\n29\t  deploy-and-manage UI.\n30\t- **Branch B — external-connection-only**: Dashboard provides per-project\n31\t  external connection registration with validated connectivity; Llama Stack\n32\t  consumes a registered connection; Dashboard connection management UI.\n33\t\n34\tAll other unclear passages (CRD shapes, wiring mechanisms, image build\n35\tstrategy, sanctioned store list) are implementation details captured as\n36\tacceptance criteria on the relevant epics, not investigations — they do not\n37\tchange which epics exist. Milvus viability/supportability is folded into the\n38\tE001 evaluation itself (same evaluation, same deliverable — not split into a\n39\tseparate investigation).\n40\t\n41\t## Epic List\n42\t\n43\t### Main plan\n44\t\n45\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n46\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n47\t| E001 | Decide first supported vector store posture (managed vs external) | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | Llama Stack | P0 |\n48\t\n49\t### Branch A — platform-managed (operator-deployed Milvus)\n50\t\n51\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n52\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n53\t| BRANCH-A-E002 | Onboard Platform Operator midstream repository | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n54\t| BRANCH-A-E003 | License validation for operator and Milvus dependency trees | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n55\t| BRANCH-A-E004 | Konflux onboarding for Platform Operator repository | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n56\t| BRANCH-A-E005 | Managed vector store deployment via Platform Operator with productized images | Implementation | RHOAI Platform | Platform Operator | P0 |\n57\t| BRANCH-A-E006 | Llama Stack RAG provider wiring for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | Llama Stack | P1 |\n58\t| BRANCH-A-E007 | Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI for the managed vector store | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard | P1 |\n59\t| BRANCH-A-E008 | Product documentation for the managed vector store posture | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | Documentation | P1 |\n60\t\n61\t### Branch B — external-connection-only\n62\t\n63\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Component | Priority |\n64\t|----|-------|------|------|-----------|----------|\n65\t| BRANCH-B-E002 | Per-project external vector store connection registration and management UI | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard