{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cc379f1fac7fcce","type":"tool_result","content":"30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 6\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Dashboard deploy-and-manage UI for the managed vector store\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tExposes the platform-managed vector store in the Dashboard: administrators\n40\tcan deploy and manage the managed vector store from the console, following\n41\tthe platform's standard component-enablement pattern for the Dashboard\n42\t(Kubernetes resource interactions plus per-component feature flags).\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Add the managed vector store to the Dashboard as an administrator-facing\n47\t  deploy-and-manage surface: triggering deployment and viewing status.\n48\t- Gate the integration behind the Dashboard's per-component feature flag\n49\t  mechanism so it can be enabled per installation.\n50\t- Interact with the managed store exclusively through its Kubernetes\n51\t  resources — the Dashboard owns no data plane and introduces no private\n52\t  component APIs.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- An administrator can trigger deployment of the managed vector store from\n57\t  the Dashboard.\n58\t- Deployment status (and failure conditions) of the managed vector store is\n59\t  visible in the Dashboard.\n60\t- The integration is disabled unless enabled through the Dashboard\n61\t  configuration's feature-flag mechanism.\n62\t- The UI operates entirely on Kubernetes resources exposed for the managed\n63\t  vector store (no new private APIs).\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: \"The Dashboard exposes the chosen integration\n68\t  (deploy-and-manage UI for the managed path)\" — managed-posture coverage.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6f2b18ba21e4e42","agent_id":"a3c9735196fff5c3d","session_id":"124e4662-1fae-4b45-93d6-fde3aa562cb7","uuid":"66