status, and deletion.\n51\t- Use productized images for the vector store components (no unqualified\n52\t  upstream tags), built through the platform build pipeline.\n53\t- Expose the deployed vector store so that platform components (Llama Stack\n54\t  distributions, Dashboard) can discover and consume it.\n55\t- Provide a clean uninstall/rollback path: removing the managed vector store\n56\t  request tears down the deployment without orphaned resources.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- An administrator can request a managed vector store through the Platform\n61\t  Operator, and the operator provisions a running vector database in the\n62\t  cluster.\n63\t- The deployed vector store is functional: a client can create collections\n64\t  and run vector search against it.\n65\t- All deployed vector store components run productized images with\n66\t  fully-qualified references (no `:latest` or unqualified upstream tags).\n67\t- The operator reconciles the resource: deletion of the request removes the\n68\t  deployment and its dependent resources cleanly.\n69\t- The build pipeline for the Platform Operator repository is green with the\n70\t  vector store changes merged (first pipeline execution gates this epic's\n71\t  completion, not its start).\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — managed-path clause: \"administrators can deploy the managed\n76\t  vector store through the Platform Operator with productized images.\"\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f7c6a191f49b2dd","agent_id":"a39a86b2524490ff1","session_id":"124e4662-1fae-4b45-93d6-fde3aa562cb7","uuid":"6a6a3cf9-9493-4a58-a4d5-79c650244380","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:13:09.908Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1a3513ab921999e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9007 revision 2"}
