 the registered connection, not manually transcribed).\n52\t- Cover the integration with tests exercising a distribution against an\n53\t  external vector store reached through a registered connection.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A Llama Stack distribution consumes a registered external vector store\n58\t  connection as its RAG vector provider with no hand-edited distribution\n59\t  configuration.\n60\t- An end-to-end RAG flow succeeds through the distribution's RAG API against\n61\t  an external vector store reached via a registered connection: documents\n62\t  are registered, embedded, and retrieved.\n63\t- Updating or removing the registered connection is reflected in the\n64\t  distribution's provider wiring without manual config edits.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: \"Llama Stack distributions can consume the chosen vector\n69\t  store as a RAG provider without hand-editing distribution configs\" —\n70\t  external-posture coverage.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f7c6a191f49b2dd","agent_id":"a39a86b2524490ff1","session_id":"124e4662-1fae-4b45-93d6-fde3aa562cb7","uuid":"7223e6f3-67d9-43bf-bd73-e27e0021c615","timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:13:25.066Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-860af2e761f230d3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9007 revision 2"}
